# ISA Returns Test Support API behaviour

The ISA Returns Test Support API is intended for organisations enrolled in the **Manage ISAs** service and is to be used
together with the ISA Returns API to support the validation of the end-to-end processing prior to deployment to the
production environment.

It is preferred to subscribe to the ISA Returns API by provisioning a valid callback URL to notify you when the sample
reconciliation report is available for download.

##End-to-end journey

The transaction lifecycle of the ISA Returns Test Support API in the sandbox environment is captured below:

<img src="images/isa-returns-test-support-end-to-end-journey.png" alt="Diagram showing the full flow of the API."
style="width:390px; max-height:364px"/>

<img src="images/isa-returns-test-support-simulated-report-generation-flow.png" alt="Diagram showing the submit report generation flow."
style="width:616px; max-height:658px"/>

The whole lifecycle via ISA Returns Test Support API is as follows:

- Initiate reconciliation report generation - The developer invokes the ISA Returns Test Support API to initiate the
generation of a reconciliation report for a specific user.
- Simulated report generation - On receipt of the request, the ISA Returns Test Support API generates a simulated
reconciliation report with sample data. The report contains error conditions corresponding to the different use cases.
- Reconciliation report availability and notification - The callback URL - provided while subscribing to the ISA
Returns API - is used to notify you when the sample reconciliation report is available for download. These notifications
are managed using the [Push Pull Notifications Service (PPNS)](https://developer.service.hmrc.gov.uk/api-documentation/docs/api/service/push-pull-notifications-api/1.0).
For more details, refer to [Notifications handling](#notifications-handling).
- Once notified of the availability of the reconciliation report, the third-party software application can subsequently
retrieve and process the report as part of the entire workflow in conjunction with the ISA Returns API.

The generated reconciliation report contains representative data and error conditions that allows the consuming
application to verify the processing and handling of the expected reconciliation outcomes without requiring the
corresponding scenario to occur in the live production environment.

### Override the reporting window

<img src="images/isa-returns-test-support-simulated-report-generation-flow.png" alt="Diagram showing the window override flow."
style="width:930px; max-height:1013px"/>

The workflow to achieve the override reporting window feature via ISA Returns Test Support API is as follows:

- Initiate override reporting window request - The developer initiates an API request from a third party application to
ISA Returns Test Support API to override the reporting window request for a specific user. The request includes the
required start date and end date for the monthly submission.
- Processes the Override request - On receipt of a valid override request, the ISA Returns Test Support API overrides
the default monthly submission reporting window and applies the requested reporting window with the specified start and
end date.
- While the override reporting window is active, there are two possible scenarios:
    - Data submitted within the default monthly submission reporting period. Once the override reporting window request
    is processed, the reporting window is open as per the new set start and end date. All data or declaration submitted
    within this period is processed successfully and a success response is sent to the third party application.
    - Data submitted outside the default monthly submission reporting period. If any data or declaration is submitted
    outside of this new start and end date, it will result in an error response which is sent to the third party
    application.

**Note**

This override feature lasts for one hour and once it expires, the default reporting window of the 6th to the 19th of
every month automatically resumes.

### Notifications handling

ISA Returns Test Support API handles the request for a simulated reconciliation report asynchronously. Consumers of the
ISA Returns API may wish to be informed once the reconciliation report is ready. This notification facility is achieved
using the PPNS, which is an API platform capability to support sending notifications to API customers.

## ISA Returns Test Support API endpoints

This API has the following endpoints:

### Generate test reconciliation report endpoint

This endpoint initiates the generation of a simulated reconciliation report with sample errors for a specific Z-reference
user. You can specify the number of simulated errors to be included for each of the
[oversubscription](reconciliation-report-handling.html#oversubscription-error-type),
[trace and match](reconciliation-report-handling.html#trace-and-match-failures) or
[ineligible investment](reconciliation-report-handling.html#eligibility-failures)
scenarios. The reconciliation report is made available to the ISA Returns API, and a notificationis triggered via
[PPNS](#notifications-handling).

**Note**

Each sample reconciliation report is limited to a maximum of 2,000 issues across all issue types per Z-reference.
Attempts to exceed this limit will result in an error.

### Override the reporting window endpoint

This endpoint provides the ability to configure a reporting window for the authenticated Z-reference. The override lasts
for one hour and once the override expires, the normal reporting-period validation resumes.

## Supported test scenarios

The ISA Returns Test Support API supports the following scenarios:

### Sample Report Generation

Use the sandbox environment to independently trigger the generation of a sample test reconciliation report. This allows
you to verify that your application can handle the entire workflow including the reconciliation reporting without
interacting with the production service.

### Reporting window override facility

Use the reporting window override feature in the sandbox environment to set a custom start and end date for the monthly
submission reporting window. This allows you to test how the ISA Returns API behaves during the monthly returns submission.
Reporting outside of the reporting window will result in an error. This override feature lasts for one hour and once it
expires, the default reporting window of the 6th to the 19th of every month automatically resumes.

### Report processing

Process the simulated reconciliation report within your application to identify integration issues before requesting
access to deploy to the production environment.

This includes validating:

- Data mapping
- Schema compatibility
- Field handling
- Reconciliation report-processing logic

Testing these scenarios in the sandbox helps identify schema mismatches and other processing issues before they affect
production workflows.

### PPNS handling

Use the sandbox environment to test the integration with the [PPNS](#notifications-handling). This allows you to verify
that your application can receive and process asynchronous events reliably as part of the reconciliation reporting
workflow.

### Error detection and handling

The ISA Returns Test Support API can simulate errors within the generated sample reconciliation reports. Use these
scenarios to validate how your application detects, handles, and responds to different error conditions before
requesting access to deploy to the production environment.

### Asynchronous processing and status handling

Use the API to support how your application interacts with the reconciliation reporting service throughout the
asynchronous report-processing lifecycle.

This includes validating:

- Asynchronous notifications
- Report availability
- Report retrieval
- Application handling of processing outcomes
